Deviations: used /tmp/lsp-eval as the build sandbox rather than the session
scratchpad. The scratchpad path contains the substring "git", which made the
worktree-isolation guard refuse several plain commands that merely mentioned it in
an environment variable; /tmp/lsp-eval is a short path with no such substring.
Nothing was installed system wide, no repository was modified, and the throwaway
plugin was never installed or enabled -- only passed to `claude plugin validate'.

Considerations: the task framing expected guile-json (GPL-3) to be the blocker, as
it was for channels in EXPERIMENTS-channels.org C8. It is not -- this chain uses
SRFI 180 and is MIT/BSD throughout. That correction is in L2, because the
licence-shaped reason to decline does not exist here and the decline rests on L13,
L12, L10 and L5 instead.

